**Read:** [Materials Processing — Chris Schuh, MIT 3.044](../sources/Materials-Processing-MIT-3-044.lingua#r_4V5BA7W1TFKGRTGNHN7ZTAK1TW), all solidification, Stefan-condition, binary-alloy, and corresponding problem/exam material; [Phase Transitions — Bhadeshia and Yan](../sources/Phase-Transitions-Bhadeshia-Yan.lingua#r_2PMPJ2B4GPGDT62S567TX1DCPJ), the complete nucleation and solidification chapters; [A Guide to the Solidification of Steels — Jernkontoret](../sources/Guide-to-Solidification-of-Steels.lingua#r_37E0W03MBAM4KMY33EF8BMT9WM), the full experimental-method and relevant alloy sections.

Solidification creates a structure through nucleation, interface motion, heat removal, solute redistribution, and flow. Equilibrium phase relations supply constitutive constraints under a stated local-equilibrium model; they do not replace energy, mass, momentum, or kinetic equations.

Derive an interface energy balance and the appropriate solute balance with compatible phase quantities and signs. Define the temperature/composition fields, latent heat, transport properties, interface behavior, and boundary/initial conditions. A moving-boundary calculation must distinguish material properties and model assumptions from parameters fitted to the same observed interface position.

Nucleation sites, undercooling, curvature, anisotropy, kinetics, thermal gradients, and fluid motion can alter morphology and phase selection. A smooth front, cellular/dendritic structure, eutectic, and multiphase casting require different levels of description. Compare model limits rather than assuming every observed pattern verifies the most elaborate simulation.

**Work:** reproduce a complete analytic or numerical solidification case from the open course and primary methods. Independently check interface/material/energy relations, limiting cases, and numerical convergence. Compare with measured thermal/structural evidence and an alternative boundary or kinetic account. Identify the observation that most discriminates the models before extending to an industrial casting with additional coupled effects.

**Continue:** [Explain solidification morphology through transport, stability, and material evidence](Front-stability-dendrites-eutectics-and-phase-selection.lingua#r_4KCQ85TBX02PBPVPS2JKGW4FMQ).

